Z||000000||WampusCat||05-09-2001||09:51 AM||||I really get annoyed by my seatbelts always getting slack in them when I drive so I constantly have to tug on them to make them retract so they are snug.  I guess all american cars from the 80's did this but is there any way to modify them to keep a constant slight tension like the belts on import cars do?||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||05-09-2001||10:25 AM||||Yeah it bothers me too! <BR>Ya know American seatbelts have always sucked In the 70's GM actually used screws to keep the seatbelts from UNBUCKELING during crash tests!! They were the older ones with the center button with the GM logo on it. <BR>Back then most people didnt use them so GM figured ahh who cares. <BR>Thank god my mine were working ok on my 79 camaro. In 87 I T boned a guy at 40mph (was going 55 when I put the binders on and slid about 50 feet) estimated. Absolutly destroyed both cars. I walked away with out a scratch. I did however have a bruise that ran from my shoulder down and across my chest. To think I had stopped just 2 minutes before hand and got a doughnut and coffee and because it was just habbit to buckel up I did it with out thinking. Prior to getting into the car I made a consious decision not to strap in! <BR>Now when I get in ANY car driving or not I feel naked if it don't strap in. <BR>Low and snug<P>Just wanted to share that <P>||||reg||8
