Z||000004||rogergarrison||05-09-2001||04:44 PM||||mine does it tool. I kinda like it. I dont like wearing them at all myself, so I like the slack when I do, dont mess up my clothes, lol. They catch all the dust from open windows, and grind a brown dirt patch across white shirts. at least they cant stop me for wearing a loose belt. Laws dont say how tite it has to be.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||05-09-2001||06:24 PM||||I don't like mine tight either.  I tug it to snap tight, then give a little tug to get it a hair off my chest.  Then it feels like I don't have it on.  Sometimes I catch myself looking down to see if it's there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>     On the other hand, if I'm going to do some ripping around, I would prefer it to be snug.  Oh well.  If you don't like it, throw some Simsons in there. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">(I wonder if they have an Earnhart edition?)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||05-09-2001||11:39 PM||||hmmm... well, speaking for Earnhardt fans, and Simpson as well I guess.. you know they found the seatbelts not at fault, as much as NASCAR tried to blame it on that. <P>Anyway...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT GT 87||05-10-2001||08:31 PM||||The Fiero belts are one of the few that would keep tight on you when you slowly lean forward , and the come back . They are considered Euro - style back in   "85 .. n Also back then most belts had a side button , not the top one that the Fiero has............. It was later shown that the side button would release early in a side collision  And now the way to go is the top button!!!!!!!!!  Steve||||reg||1
